   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "LONG-FORM CHAIN - render ONE LINK PER QUEUE RUN.\n\nPER LINK:\n  1. set link_index on H3 Long-form Links (0, 1, 2, 3 ...)\n  2. set offset_seconds on H3 Audio Lock = link_index x 15.08\n  3. LINK 0 only: bypass the LoadImage + H3 Chain Frame nodes (select, Ctrl+B)\n     LINK 1+:      save the previous render's LAST FRAME and load it there\n  4. queue. Assemble the clips end to end afterwards - no trimming, no overlap.\n\nWHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY (docs/long-form-waves.md):\n  - HEAD and TAIL are byte-identical on every link and the clause carries the\n    change. Each link is generated INDEPENDENTLY; relative wording made the\n    early chains incoherent.\n  - SAME SEED on every link. The seed output is wired into RandomNoise so this\n    is not something you have to remember.\n  - Keyframe = previous link's LAST FRAME, present_keyframe ON. That is the only\n    continuation mechanism that does not cut or ping-pong.\n  - NO latent pin and NO tail video reference. The pin cuts at its boundary; a\n    reference converges the ending onto itself. Nine waves, both inseparable\n    from their side effects.\n  - ONE soundtrack for the whole take, sliced by offset_seconds. Generating\n    audio per link restarts the music every link; pinning the SAME slice into\n    every link loops it. Build a 60s track first (H3 Audio Prompt at 32x32).\n  - 640x1120. 768x1152 produced cuts in chained clips with all else equal.\n\nKNOWN DEFECT: a still frame carries pose but not velocity, so motion can resume\nat the wrong speed. Every mechanism that carries velocity is a reference, and\nreferences converge. Unsolved."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
